# Sprint 3 Review

## Objective

To implement administrator order management functionality within the Leaf & Root e-commerce system by providing a secure administrative interface for viewing, searching and managing customer orders.

## Completed Features

### Order Management

- Order Management Controller
- Admin Order Listing
- Order Details Viewing
- Order Status Updates
- Order Status Management Interface
- Order Status Validation

### Order Search

- Search Orders by Order ID
- Search Orders by First Name
- Search Orders by Last Name
- Search Orders by Email Address
- Search Result Filtering
- Search Query Persistence

### Order Details

- Customer Details Display
- Delivery Address Display
- Order Item Display
- Quantity Display
- Unit Price Display
- Order Subtotal Display
- Order Total Display
- Current Order Status Display

### Administrative Interface Improvements

- Manage Orders Navigation Link
- Order Status Badges
- Order Status Update Form
- Success Flash Messages
- Paginated Order Listing

### Architecture & Quality Improvements

- Dedicated Order Management Controller
- Dedicated UpdateOrderStatusRequest Validation
- Eloquent Search Scope
- OrderStatus Backed Enum
- Enum-Based Status Badge Styling
- Enum Validation Rules
- Eager Loading of Order Items and Products
- SQL Wildcard Safe Search Handling
- Strongly Typed Model Relationships
- Improved Model Casting

## Outcome

Administrators can successfully access a dedicated Order Management area, view customer orders, search for specific orders, review detailed customer and delivery information, inspect purchased products and update order statuses throughout the fulfilment process.

Order information is displayed through a structured administrative interface with pagination, search functionality and status indicators. Status updates are validated and stored successfully, allowing administrators to track order progress from Pending through to Completed or Cancelled.

The implementation provides a complete order management workflow that complements the customer ordering functionality developed during Sprint 2 and improves operational visibility within the administrative area.

## Sprint Result

Successful